WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:23.917
Gerald and Kathleen were certain that the white towers belonged to an enchanted castle.

2
00:00:23.918 --> 00:00:29.417
Jimmy was not so sure.

3
00:00:29.418 --> 00:00:37.419
They walked through a beautiful garden until they came to a maze.

4
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:43.519
They tried to find the center of the maze.

5
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.929
But it was impossible!

6
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:51.302
"What's that?" Gerald picked up a red thread on the ground.

7
00:00:51.303 --> 00:00:55.887
One end was tied to a thimble, but the other end . . .

8
00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:59.729
"There is no other end!" Gerald realized.

9
00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.101
"Maybe it leads to something!"

10
00:01:02.102 --> 00:01:06.717
"I think the gardener put it there," said Jimmy.

11
00:01:06.718 --> 00:01:10.922
"Look at the crown on that thimble," said Kathleen.

12
00:01:10.923 --> 00:01:15.489
"Do you think a gardener would have a princess' silver thimble?"

13
00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.057
"Let's follow the thread."

14
00:01:17.058 --> 00:01:22.167
Gerald walked forward, winding the thread around his fingers as he went.

15
00:01:22.168 --> 00:01:26.046
The thread led them into the middle of the maze.

16
00:01:26.047 --> 00:01:30.963
There they found a circle of green lawn with a sundial in the center.

17
00:01:30.964 --> 00:01:36.230
All around the edge of the circle was a marble seat.

18
00:01:36.231 --> 00:01:39.258
The thread ran across the lawn.

19
00:01:39.259 --> 00:01:46.468
It ended in the hand of someone sleeping on the seat!

20
00:01:46.469 --> 00:01:50.237
"It's an enchanted princess!" said Gerald.

21
00:01:50.238 --> 00:01:55.159
"Her clothes are so old-fashioned," said Kathleen.

22
00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:59.440
"She must have fallen asleep a hundred years ago."

23
00:01:59.441 --> 00:02:03.918
"She isn't really a princess," said Jimmy.

24
00:02:03.919 --> 00:02:08.054
Gerald and Kathleen laughed.

25
00:02:08.055 --> 00:02:11.249
They didn't care what Jimmy said.

26
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:17.606
Every part of the adventure—the cave, the maze, the thread—felt magical to them.

27
00:02:17.607 --> 00:02:21.566
"Lift up the veil, Gerald," whispered Kathleen.

28
00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:26.618
"If she's beautiful, we'll know she's a princess."

29
00:02:26.619 --> 00:02:29.914
"Lift it yourself," he said.

30
00:02:29.915 --> 00:02:32.862
Kathleen gently lifted the veil.

31
00:02:32.863 --> 00:02:35.759
"Isn't she lovely?"

32
00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.103
"Not too bad," Gerald muttered.

33
00:02:39.104 --> 00:02:45.132
"Now, Gerald, you must wake the princess," said Kathleen.

34
00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:49.218
"She's not a princess," insisted Jimmy.

35
00:02:49.219 --> 00:02:52.595
"She's only a little girl dressed up like a princess.

36
00:02:52.596 --> 00:02:54.647
Look at how long her dress is.

37
00:02:54.648 --> 00:02:58.622
She won't be any taller than Gerald when she stands up."

38
00:02:58.623 --> 00:03:00.687
Kathleen ignored him.

39
00:03:00.688 --> 00:03:03.054
"Gerald, you're the oldest.

40
00:03:03.055 --> 00:03:05.745
You have to kiss her awake."

41
00:03:05.746 --> 00:03:08.512
"Not me!" cried Gerald.

42
00:03:08.513 --> 00:03:11.191
"She'll slap me the minute she wakes up."

43
00:03:11.192 --> 00:03:14.695
"Then I'll do it," said Kathleen.

44
00:03:14.696 --> 00:03:16.983
"But I don't think it'll do any good."

45
00:03:16.984 --> 00:03:20.205
And it didn't.

46
00:03:20.206 --> 00:03:23.431
"I don't mind kissing her," said Jimmy.

47
00:03:23.432 --> 00:03:26.938
"I'm not afraid like some people."

48
00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:31.810
With that, Jimmy planted a loud kiss on the princess' cheek.

49
00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:36.216
The three children stood waiting to see what would happen next.

50
00:03:36.217 --> 00:03:39.686
The princess opened her large, dark eyes.

51
00:03:39.687 --> 00:03:44.863
She stretched her arms and yawned.

52
00:03:44.864 --> 00:03:50.635
Then she said, "So the hundred years are over?

53
00:03:50.636 --> 00:03:54.368
Which one of you is my hero?"

54
00:03:54.369 --> 00:03:57.178
"I am," said Jimmy.

55
00:03:57.179 --> 00:04:04.089
"My prince." The princess held out her hand and Jimmy shook it hard.

56
00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:09.387
"But you aren't really a princess, are you?" he asked.

57
00:04:09.388 --> 00:04:10.972
"Of course I am.

58
00:04:10.973 --> 00:04:12.537
Look at my crown."

59
00:04:12.538 --> 00:04:17.922
She pulled aside her veil to reveal a crown of diamonds.

60
00:04:17.923 --> 00:04:21.722
"How did you ever get past the dragons?"

61
00:04:21.723 --> 00:04:24.212
Gerald ignored her question.

62
00:04:24.213 --> 00:04:27.418
"Then this really is an enchanted castle?"

63
00:04:27.419 --> 00:04:31.555
"Of course it is. Don't be stupid."

64
00:04:31.556 --> 00:04:36.001
The princess stood up and her dress fell in waves around her feet.

65
00:04:36.002 --> 00:04:40.431
"I told you her dress would be too long," said Jimmy.

66
00:04:40.432 --> 00:04:44.645
"It must have grown over the years," said the princess.

67
00:04:44.646 --> 00:04:48.872
"Let's go back to the castle, and I'll show you all my lovely jewels.

68
00:04:48.873 --> 00:04:50.515
Would you like that?"

69
00:04:50.516 --> 00:04:54.676
"Yes," said Gerald. "But . . ."

70
00:04:54.677 --> 00:04:58.865
"But what?" The princess sounded impatient.

71
00:04:58.866 --> 00:05:00.602
"But we're awfully hungry.

72
00:05:00.603 --> 00:05:03.213
We never got to eat our lunch."

73
00:05:03.214 --> 00:05:05.684
The princess looked at the sundial.

74
00:05:05.685 --> 00:05:07.721
It was three o'clock.

75
00:05:07.722 --> 00:05:10.102
"You've had nothing to eat for hours.

76
00:05:10.103 --> 00:05:11.212
But think of me.

77
00:05:11.213 --> 00:05:18.006
I've had nothing to eat for a hundred years!"
